  "pr": {
    "description": "### Overview\\nPre-BRIEF-3 cleanup: a shared **types-only** workspace package (\`packages/types\`) so every package stops re-declaring \`ValueOf\`/\`Result\`/\`Brand\`/\`MaybePromise\` locally. Zero runtime exports and zero dependencies — the guarantee that makes it safe for \`github\` (no-DB-imports rule) and everyone else to depend on. Room for shared domain types later.\\n\\nStacked on #27 (PR D of the BRIEF-2 stack); retarget to main as the stack merges.\\n\\n### Changelog\\n- New \`packages/types\` (lib.ts + AGENTS.md documenting the types-only/zero-deps invariants)\\n- persistence: imports + re-exports the shared types; public contract unchanged; crypto.ts local \`MaybePromise\` removed\\n- github: \`src/types.ts\` becomes a re-export; AGENTS.md local-copies rule rewritten\\n- api: \`RefreshErrorCode\` uses \`ValueOf\`\\n- apps/web: \`brief/types.ts\` re-exports \`ValueOf\` (existing \`./types\` import sites unchanged)\\n- CI: \`packages/types/\` changes trigger all dependent package jobs",
